# Finish means push origin main

Work only on `main`. At the start of any work in this repo, check out `main` and pull `origin/main` before the first edit. Stay on `main`. Do not create a feature branch.

A change is not done until `git push origin main`. Railway (`https://books.spodazo.com`) deploys from `main` only. A local commit that has not been pushed is not live.

Finish in the same turn: implement, verify, commit on `main`, then `git push origin main`. No pull request. No merge step. Do not stop after a local commit and ask whether to publish.

When they say `pp`, that is the same publish step if the push has not happened yet. Do not ask for extra confirmation.

Never force-push `main`. Never update git config. Never skip hooks.
